            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed both added files in full. Has performs no writes and treats a missing store as absent, so a read-only or never-written state home degrades gracefully. Add is retry-safe because statestore.Publish is documented as idempotent, and the second-Add test covers it. Link and symlink refusals surface as wrapped errors and are tested. Keys are length-bounded and character-restricted, and each operation does one directory check plus one small bounded read or write, so there is no unbounded latency or load. Errors are wrapped with the store name, which gives adequate observability. I found no concrete production failure mode caused by this candidate."
            ]
          }
